/**
  @page examples-mmg-mesh_optimization Improving triangle quality
  @brief Remesh a perturbed unit square and inspect its cell quality.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-intro Geometry and objective

  A nine-by-nine vertex grid is scaled to the unit square. Small interior
  coordinate perturbations create uneven triangles while the square boundary
  and its corner positions are retained. MMG optimization changes the mesh
  connectivity and coordinates to improve element quality near the existing
  size distribution.

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-basic Prepare and optimize

  Boundary incidence is prepared before geometric features are marked.
  Corner indices follow the generated grid's vertex ordering.

  @snippet MMG/MeshOptimization.cpp mmg-optimizer-setup
  @snippet MMG/MeshOptimization.cpp mmg-optimizer-call

  Finite element spaces and algebraic problems should be constructed again
  after remeshing. Indices and connectivity can change during this operation.

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-params Size and geometry settings

  | Setting | Role |
  | :--- | :--- |
  | `setHMin(h)` | Lower requested edge-size bound |
  | `setHMax(h)` | Upper requested edge-size bound |
  | `setHausdorff(h)` | Geometric approximation tolerance |
  | `setAngleDetection(enabled)` | Automatic sharp-feature detection |

  The example uses size bounds 0.05 and 0.2 on a unit square. These settings
  should be scaled with the physical domain and its required geometric detail.
  A spatially varying size field is supplied through
  @ref examples-mmg-mesh_adaptation "metric adaptation".

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-required Required geometry

  Required entities and sharp features have operation-specific preservation
  behavior. See @ref examples-mmg-behavior-required before relying on a
  particular vertex, edge or face surviving a remesh or a level-set cut.

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-results Inspect the result

  @m_class{rodin-mesh-stages}

  @parblock
  @image html MMGOptimization-before.png "Mesh before optimization, with the same plotting scale."
  @image html MMGOptimization-after.png "Mesh after optimization, with the same plotting scale."
  @endparblock

  For a triangle with area @f$A@f$ and edge lengths @f$\ell_i@f$, the example
  reports the normalized shape measure
  @f[
    q=\frac{4\sqrt{3}A}{\ell_1^2+\ell_2^2+\ell_3^2}.
  @f]
  An equilateral triangle has value one; degenerate triangles approach zero.
  The local run increased the minimum from approximately 0.492 to 0.787,
  with 128 input triangles and 124 output triangles. The domain area remained
  one. These measurements describe this input and MMG build.

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-full Build and run

  Build the `MeshOptimization` target. It writes `Before.medit.mesh`,
  `After.medit.mesh` and corresponding triangle CSV files. The program checks
  positive cell measures and unit total area with tolerance @f$10^{-10}@f$.

  The complete program is available in @ref MMG/MeshOptimization.cpp "MeshOptimization.cpp".

  @section examples-mmg-meshopt-see-also Continue

  - @ref examples-mmg-simple_io "MMG mesh and feature I/O"
  - @ref examples-mmg-mesh_adaptation "Prescribe local sizes"
  - @ref examples-mmg-behavior "Preservation behavior"

  @example MMG/MeshOptimization.cpp
  @m_examplenavigation{examples-mmg-mesh_optimization,MMG/}
  @m_footernavigation
*/
